WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.423 --> 00:00:05.423
(dubstep music)

00:00:14.773 --> 00:00:18.314
- No offense, but air quality
in China is not great.

00:00:18.314 --> 00:00:20.529
People are actually buying
bottled Canadian air

00:00:20.529 --> 00:00:22.026
for big bucks.

00:00:22.026 --> 00:00:23.571
LA air is crap too.

00:00:23.571 --> 00:00:27.538
We've got a natural-gas leak
that won't be fixed for months.

00:00:27.538 --> 00:00:30.162
People here love to be organic AF,

00:00:30.162 --> 00:00:33.831
so I've come up with an ingenious
product for LA citizens:

00:00:33.831 --> 00:00:35.422
artisanal air,

00:00:35.422 --> 00:00:38.173
fresh, organic, single-sourced.

00:00:38.173 --> 00:00:39.508
Take a whiff;

00:00:39.508 --> 00:00:41.063
you deserve it.

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:46.808
- Oh, you wanna sit in that chair?

00:00:46.808 --> 00:00:47.969
Cool, me too.

00:00:47.969 --> 00:00:49.014
Actually I don't like sharing.

00:00:49.014 --> 00:00:51.345
Get the (beeping) out of my chair.

00:00:51.345 --> 00:00:52.386
(cat meowing)

00:00:52.386 --> 00:00:53.513
- It's the new year.

00:00:53.513 --> 00:00:55.008
I wanna be eating more vegetables.

00:00:55.008 --> 00:00:56.810
I want them to be super-colorful;

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:58.934
so I came to a grilled cheese place

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:01.152
to make the most colorful
grilled cheese sandwich

00:01:01.152 --> 00:01:02.734
I could ever make.

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:05.817
- [Man] We'll start with red peppers.

00:01:05.817 --> 00:01:07.788
Ah! Carrot slaw, carrot slaw.

00:01:07.788 --> 00:01:08.705
American cheese?
- [Lynn] Yeah!

00:01:08.705 --> 00:01:09.694
Arugula?

00:01:09.694 --> 00:01:11.266
- [Lynn] Root for spice?

00:01:11.266 --> 00:01:12.623
- [Eric] Is it possible
- [Lynn] Do you...

00:01:12.623 --> 00:01:15.003
In the world of food?
But you have blue cheese.

00:01:15.003 --> 00:01:17.706
What we do is we make
a blue-cheese spread.

00:01:17.706 --> 00:01:22.706
(spry lively orchestral music)

00:01:23.511 --> 00:01:26.889
(sizzling)

00:01:26.889 --> 00:01:31.889
(spry lively orchestral music)

00:01:31.936 --> 00:01:33.352
- [Lynn] What just happened here?

00:01:33.352 --> 00:01:35.349
I asked for vegetables.

00:01:35.349 --> 00:01:36.975
I got a grilled cheese sandwich.

00:01:36.975 --> 00:01:38.144
- That happens around me.

00:01:38.144 --> 00:01:41.232
- [Lynn] This is the pot of
gold at the end of the rainbow.

00:01:41.232 --> 00:01:44.692
So for those of you trying to
eat more vegetables in 2016,

00:01:44.692 --> 00:01:48.613
I highly recommend doing
it in grilled-cheese form.

00:01:48.613 --> 00:01:50.622
- [Man] Gavon, was today
a good day or bad day?

00:01:50.622 --> 00:01:52.160
- Oh!

00:01:55.209 --> 00:01:56.328
It was a good day!

00:01:56.328 --> 00:01:57.114
- [Man] Why?

00:01:57.114 --> 00:01:59.961
- Well first of all, North Korea claims

00:01:59.961 --> 00:02:02.585
they tested an H-bomb,
but I'm not convinced

00:02:02.585 --> 00:02:05.510
it's anything other than
a viral promotional stunt

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:06.913
for the next Godzilla movie.

00:02:06.913 --> 00:02:08.715
There was a press conference in Oregon

00:02:08.715 --> 00:02:10.433
by a Native American tribe

00:02:10.433 --> 00:02:11.927
who thought it was pretty rich

00:02:11.927 --> 00:02:14.673
that all of these white
European dudes in beards

00:02:14.673 --> 00:02:17.732
are claiming they are the
original owners of the land.

00:02:17.732 --> 00:02:19.265
Also there's a big puddle in England

00:02:19.265 --> 00:02:21.064
that everybody's freaking out about.

00:02:21.064 --> 00:02:22.687
So all in all, a banner day.

00:02:22.687 --> 00:02:23.987
- [Man] (laughing)

00:02:23.987 --> 00:02:28.987
(funky electronic music)

